WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.626
The paper makes three contributions.

00:00:03.706 --> 00:00:07.331
First,

00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:11.037
it corrects two misconceptions: CCS classifies
using only the displacement between a statement and its negation,

00:00:11.117 --> 00:00:14.743
needing no separating hyperplane,

00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:18.449
and succeeds even when probabilities cluster near
one half.

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:22.154
Second, it derives a new Midpoint-Displacement loss.

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:25.860
Third, a comparison shows it proxies, and can beat, CCS.
